{"id":"chatcmpl-18f92fee-8881-4537-b578-e637e0240779","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229411,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task required distinguishing between left and right lower lobe atelectasis on a chest X-ray. The successful strategy combined a focused expert interpretation query (asking specifically about side and lobe) with a grounded localization report to cross-verify the finding. The key abstraction is to decompose a binary laterality question into targeted sub-queries that explicitly request side/location, then corroborate with a second independent localization source.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question asks to choose between two lateralized findings (left vs right), explicitly query the interpretation tool for side and lobe rather than a generic 'is there atelectasis' question.\",\n    \"Pair a focused expert-QA call with a grounded/localized report call so that the final answer is corroborated by two independent evidence sources.\",\n    \"Decompose the diagnostic question into the specific attributes being discriminated (side, lobe, opacity type) before invoking tools, so each tool call targets the decision boundary.\",\n    \"Use the grounded report to obtain localized visual evidence that can confirm or override the expert-QA impression when laterality is the deciding factor.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging laterality questions\": \"Always ask the expert tool explicitly for patient left vs right and lobe; never rely on a generic presence/absence query when the options differ only by side.\",\n    \"Binary-choice diagnostic tasks\": \"Identify the single discriminating attribute between options (here: side), then design tool queries that directly resolve that attribute.\",\n    \"Multi-tool corroboration\": \"Combine a high-level expert interpretation with a grounded/localized report; agreement across both raises confidence before committing to an answer.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the tool query explicitly names the discriminating attribute (side and lobe) rather than asking only about presence of the finding.\",\n    \"Verify the grounded report's localization agrees with the expert interpretation's stated side before selecting the final option.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":505,"total_tokens":907,"completion_tokens":402,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":505},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":402}}}